## Founding & History
Glendale Estate is a historic property in Tasmania's Tamar Valley, with original timber buildings dating back to the late 19th century. It was established as an apple orchard in 1892. The property was later converted into a vineyard by its current owners, Chris and Cassie Payne. The old apple packing shed, built in the 1920s, has been restored and repurposed as the cellar door and an event hall. The Payne family purchased the vineyard in Sidmouth, with buildings from the 1800s, and submitted an offer on the same day they viewed it. The winery itself was established in 2019.

## People
Glendale Vineyard is owned and operated by Chris and Cassie Payne. Chris Payne serves as both the viticulturist and winemaker for Glendale Estate. Cassie Payne tends to the garden and is involved in arranging special events at the cellar door. The couple moved from high-pressure corporate jobs in Los Angeles to pursue a simpler life in Tasmania. They have four children: Leo, Lennox, Lulu, and Ziggy.

## Vineyard & Site
Glendale Estate is situated in the heart of Tasmania's Tamar Valley, surrounded by rolling hills, farmland, and vines. The vineyard has 2.8 hectares planted. The winemaking approach at Glendale begins in the vineyard, with careful attention paid to the soil and grape development. Tasmania experiences a long, cool growing season with sometimes unpredictable weather, which necessitates an ongoing dialogue between the viticulturist and the vines. All of Glendale's wines are single vineyard, estate grown, and made. The estate takes a holistic approach to farming.

## Cellar Door Experience
The cellar door at Glendale Estate is housed in a restored 1920s apple packing shed. It offers a warm and intimate setting for wine tastings. Visitors can enjoy a thoroughly guided personalized wine tasting by staff or explore self-guided wine flights. Options include a vertical Pinot Noir flight of five wines or a mixed wine flight of five wines, each priced at $15 per tasting. Bookings are recommended for all tasting experiences to ensure a personalized visit. During autumn, the cellar door is open on Saturdays from 11 am to 4 pm. Other sources indicate summer hours are daily, and autumn/winter hours are Friday through Monday from 11 am to 4 pm, closed Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with a note to check for private functions. The cellar door is closed on Christmas Day. It is described as a place to relax by the fire while tasting wines.

## Food & Hospitality
Glendale Estate offers wine and cheese pairings featuring locally sourced Tasmanian artisanal produce, designed to complement their wines. These pairings can change seasonally or weekly based on available produce and local cheeses. The estate hosts family-friendly events with live music during summer. In winter, the cellar door provides a cozy atmosphere by the fire. The Orchard Shed, a restored barn-style venue, is available for weddings and private events, with picturesque locations overlooking the vineyard, a dam, and surrounding mountains. The venue can accommodate up to 200 guests for weddings.

## Awards & Recognition
Glendale Estate has received specific ratings for some of its wines from the Halliday Wine Companion. The Glendale Estate Rosé 2023 Tasmania received 92 points (silver). The Glendale Estate Blanc de Noir 2021 Sparkling | Tasmania also received 92 points (silver). The Glendale Estate Pinot Noir 2021 Tasmania was awarded 93 points (silver).

## Sustainability & Certifications
Glendale Estate's dedication to sustainable practices is noted. While specific certifications are not explicitly mentioned in the provided search results, Wine Tasmania operates a VinØ ('vin zero') Program, which helps wine producers implement sustainable practices. Glendale Estate is listed as a Wine Producer Member of Wine Tasmania.

## Visiting Practical Info
The address for Glendale Estate Vineyard is 163 Glendale Road, Sidmouth, TAS 7270, Australia. The phone number is 0488 033 492. The website is glendaletasmania.com. The vineyard is located approximately half an hour from Launceston. It is also conveniently located about 10 minutes from shopping and schools. The estate is part of the Tamar Valley Wine Route. Social media presence includes Facebook and Instagram. The cellar door is currently closed for renovations over winter.

## Notable / Distinctive
Glendale Estate is distinctive for its history as a late 19th-century apple orchard, with its cellar door housed in a lovingly restored 1920s apple packing shed. The property's original timber buildings have been preserved. The owners, Chris and Cassie Payne, transitioned from high-pressure corporate jobs in Los Angeles to establish their vineyard in Tasmania, with Chris originally from the region. The winery offers vertical tastings of its Pinot Noir and Chardonnay, with vintages dating back to 2012. It is a family-owned and operated winery that focuses on small-batch, handcrafted wines with minimal intervention. The estate also serves as a wedding and event venue, utilizing its historic buildings and scenic views.

